// M5-A3P-1014. Ending E4 "The Kite comes down" (E, 2 min). No person's goodbye: THE MACHINES, the cost
// to the Saltwrights. act3_ending.md §2 E4. The glide runs out. Liss brings it down onto the water BY HAND, with ropes
// and the sails Dace modelled on Virel. One player input: hold to take the strain with her. Sweat, rope, darkness; a
// hard landing that everyone survives. LISS DOESN'T CRY UNTIL IT'S DOWN. T-09 (proposed): an insert of Tobin's lamp,
// dark in its socket. `silence`: only wind, rope creak, and the hull meeting water.
title: ending_the_kite_comes_down
location: ch18/kite
---
@music silence fade=0.0
@mark liss kite_wheel walk
@sfx wind_in_sails
@wait 4.0
<<event hold_input take_the_strain>>
@anim liss haul sheet_rope
@sfx rope_creak
@wait 6.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@sfx hull_meets_water
@wait 3.0
@camera E09
@wait 3.0
@anim liss cry
@wait 6.0
===
